WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.650
Start in Learn. Choose the topic your teacher
has set, or the

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.588
one you need to strengthen.

3
00:00:06.738 --> 00:00:12.123
New to chemical calculations? Begin with mass,
moles and particles. Use the

4
00:00:12.123 --> 00:00:16.611
chapter buttons to jump straight to the help you
need.

5
00:00:16.761 --> 00:00:21.949
Use the explained model to understand why each
step was chosen. Keep

6
00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:24.110
paper and a calculator nearby.

7
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:29.027
Pause after a line and explain the decision in
your own words.

8
00:00:29.027 --> 00:00:31.013
Then try the supported question.

9
00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:35.851
Complete the missing step starts you with some
working already supplied. Your

10
00:00:35.851 --> 00:00:38.586
job is to finish the next part.

11
00:00:38.736 --> 00:00:44.389
Try first, then select Check my working. Stuck?
Use I need a

12
00:00:44.389 --> 00:00:48.629
hint, read the prompt, and try the step again.

13
00:00:48.779 --> 00:00:53.065
A more explicit hint gives further guidance.
Show the full method is

14
00:00:53.065 --> 00:00:55.923
a separate choice if you still need it.

15
00:00:56.073 --> 00:01:01.500
Then try with fewer prompts, or move to a fresh
independent question.

16
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.666
Hints carry no mark penalty during practice.

17
00:01:04.816 --> 00:01:09.893
In Mole lab, predict what will change before
changing a mass or

18
00:01:09.893 --> 00:01:12.854
substance. Compare the result with your
prediction.

19
00:01:13.004 --> 00:01:18.007
In Solutions, change the amount of solute and
watch the representative ion

20
00:01:18.007 --> 00:01:23.010
counts change. Hold the amount fixed and change
volume: the water level

21
00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:26.346
changes, but the ion counts stay the same.

22
00:01:26.496 --> 00:01:32.090
Reveal concentrations shows the result and the
working. Explain what changed, and

23
00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.954
what stayed the same.

24
00:01:34.104 --> 00:01:40.470
Reaction lab compares reactants, products and
excess. Predict which reactant runs out

25
00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.592
before revealing the reaction.

26
00:01:42.742 --> 00:01:47.315
Build a method helps when choosing the route is
the difficult part.

27
00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:51.125
Start with the given quantity and identify the
requested quantity.

28
00:01:51.275 --> 00:01:55.708
Choose your route and check it, then complete
each step. Use the

29
00:01:55.708 --> 00:01:59.033
checklist or the full method when you need
support.

30
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:03.996
In Practise, choose a topic and work on paper
before entering an

31
00:02:03.996 --> 00:02:07.606
answer. Check the feedback and correct a
specific error.

32
00:02:07.756 --> 00:02:12.599
Use Hint or Worked solution if needed, then try
another question. A

33
00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:17.442
correct practice answer is a useful step, not
proof you can do

34
00:02:17.442 --> 00:02:18.653
every version independently.

35
00:02:18.803 --> 00:02:23.245
Check and review gives you a fresh question with
the model and

36
00:02:23.245 --> 00:02:26.576
hints closed. Write your method before entering
your answers.

37
00:02:26.726 --> 00:02:32.440
Select the units and explain your decision.
Submit my check reveals feedback.

38
00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.249
If you need help first, return to learning.

39
00:02:36.399 --> 00:02:41.484
These checks stay in your studio learning
record. They do not automatically

40
00:02:41.484 --> 00:02:44.027
become marks in the Canvas gradebook.

41
00:02:44.177 --> 00:02:49.391
Open Canvas checkpoints in this studio. Choose
Pilot A for automatic questions,

42
00:02:49.391 --> 00:02:54.604
Pilot B for mixed reasoning, or Pilot C for
written working. Sign

43
00:02:54.604 --> 00:02:58.080
in to your school Canvas account if asked.

44
00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:03.219
These are exam-practice pilots. They do not
count towards your official term

45
00:03:03.219 --> 00:03:08.209
mark. Canvas records results for teacher review;
results are being held and

46
00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:11.951
are not being released to parents during this
pilot.

47
00:03:12.101 --> 00:03:17.018
For a quiz, read the instructions, select Take
the quiz, answer every

48
00:03:17.018 --> 00:03:21.936
question, then select Submit quiz at the end. A
muted-score message means

49
00:03:21.936 --> 00:03:26.853
your result is being held for review; it does
not mean submission

50
00:03:26.853 --> 00:03:27.263
failed.

51
00:03:27.413 --> 00:03:32.719
For Pilot C, complete both tasks on paper.
Photograph the whole page

52
00:03:32.719 --> 00:03:38.024
clearly or save it as a PDF. At the top of the

53
00:03:38.024 --> 00:03:40.235
Canvas assignment, select Start Assignment.

54
00:03:40.385 --> 00:03:45.450
In File upload, select Choose a file to upload
and choose your

55
00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:50.516
photo or PDF. On a smaller screen, scroll down
to find these

56
00:03:50.516 --> 00:03:50.938
controls.

57
00:03:51.088 --> 00:03:56.007
Check that your file appears. Selecting it is
not the final step:

58
00:03:56.007 --> 00:04:00.516
now press the blue Submit assignment button
below the upload box.

59
00:04:00.666 --> 00:04:05.587
Wait for Submitted and a submission time. Open
Submission details to check

60
00:04:05.587 --> 00:04:10.508
the right file arrived. New Attempt lets you
send a corrected version

61
00:04:10.508 --> 00:04:12.148
during this practice pilot.

62
00:04:12.298 --> 00:04:17.018
You can also choose Text entry after Start
Assignment. Type or paste

63
00:04:17.018 --> 00:04:21.737
your method in the main editor, then press
Submit assignment. The small

64
00:04:21.737 --> 00:04:25.670
Comments box is for a note, not your main
answer.

65
00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:31.108
These screens use Canvas Test Student. Your
teacher will review written working

66
00:04:31.108 --> 00:04:36.396
with the rubric. Use the studio hints for
learning, and complete your

67
00:04:36.396 --> 00:04:37.718
Canvas attempt independently.

68
00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:42.644
Return after a gap and try fresh questions. Your
learning record stays

69
00:04:42.644 --> 00:04:47.421
in this browser on this device, so download a
copy if needed.

70
00:04:47.571 --> 00:04:52.656
Feedback and downloads lets you copy your notes,
download them, or keep

71
00:04:52.656 --> 00:04:55.199
a standalone copy of the studio.

72
00:04:55.349 --> 00:05:00.414
Open the downloaded studio in a web browser.
Videos may need a

73
00:05:00.414 --> 00:05:02.947
separate download or an internet connection.

74
00:05:03.097 --> 00:05:07.927
Use captions if you cannot hear a video. Check
the player volume

75
00:05:07.927 --> 00:05:12.355
or open its separate link. Replay just the
chapter you need.
